==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hvat|lang=is}}, originally the neuter form of {{recons|hver|lang=non}} (from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|hwaz|lang=gem-pro}}), but conflated with {{term|hverr|lang=non}} (whence Modern Icelandic {{term|hver|lang=is}}). Corresponds to {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|hwat|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|kʷód|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|kʷod|lang=ine-pro}}. See {{term|hver|lang=is}}.

